{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "504733ce-a6e6-8a2f-87de-9e311fa5ac59",
  "created_at": "2026-02-10T10:50:51-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Zoning and Inspections",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Janice Sherman",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Anita Chaudhry",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-10T10:49:07-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Zoning and Inspections, this is Anita. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-10T10:49:11-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, hello. I am calling about a fence. I have a house on Pelham Street, one-eighteen Pelham Street, one-eighteen. The old fence is rotted, very bad, so I want to put new one in same spot."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-10T10:49:23-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, so a replacement, same location as the old one. What are you planning to build it out of, and how tall?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-10T10:49:30-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Cedar wood. Five feet tall, five feet. Is this okay? What are the rules for fence? I need some paper for this, a permit?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-10T10:49:38-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Generally, yes, a fence usually needs a permit, and a replacement can still count. Since you're in the Historic Hill area, there may be an extra review too. Is the old fence on the property line or inside it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-10T10:49:51-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I think on the line. Maybe inside little bit. I am not sure. Sorry, I do not understand the line thing very well."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-10T10:49:59-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's all right. A survey or plot plan would show it. Do you have one from when you bought the house?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-10T10:50:06-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Maybe in the file. I will look. And the neighbor, I must tell the neighbor? Must notify him, or not?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-10T10:50:13-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can't say for certain whether notice is required in your case. I'll have the permit staff confirm that. Can I take your number and have someone call you back?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-10T10:50:23-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, yes. Four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-nine-four. Zero-one-nine-four."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-10T10:50:26-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, four-oh-one, five-five-five, zero-one-nine-four. Is that your home line?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-10T10:50:30-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, home. Not cell. My cell, sometimes my car bluetooth connect to the wrong phone, so I cannot hear, so better the home number."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-10T10:50:38-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood, home it is. Someone will call you back about the permit and the neighbor question. Look for that survey in the meantime."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-10T10:50:46-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So permit, probably yes, and neighbor, they will tell me. Thank you, thank you."
    }
  ],
